# WhatsApp group tiers — which groups the Radar reads and how closely

Keyed by JID (the long number@g.us) because several groups share a name. Move a line between tiers any time; the next export ships the change.
setup.command adds every group it finds under **U — Untiered**; the onboarding chat sorts them into A/B/C/D. New groups you join later land in U automatically (treated like B until you move them).

## A — Core (summarize fully: deadlines, events, announcements, anything addressed to you)
Class-wide, section, cohort, course and housing groups.

## B — Workstream / career / close circle (extract people, opportunities, asks; don't miss anything substantive)
Clubs you're active in, career groups, small dinner/trip groups, anything tied to what you're working on.

## C — Interest / social (one line each: only events, sign-ups, deadlines)
Sports, food, parties, travel, hobby groups.

## D — Ignore
Photo dumps, buy/sell, anything you never want to see here.

## X — Not GSB (skip)
Family, work, non-school groups. Never exported.

## U — Untiered (new, not yet classified; read like B until you move them)

## Classification rules (for the weekly scan and the onboarding chat)
- A: class-wide / section / cohort-wide official or admin groups, course and squad groups, housing/residence groups.
- B: clubs and workstream groups, career/job groups, close-circle groups (cabin, small group dinners, trip planning you organize).
- C: interest and social groups (sports, food, parties, treks you're not organizing).
- D: photo-only, buy/sell/trade, anything explicitly muted forever.
- X: not GSB at all.
- When unsure, pick the higher-coverage tier (A > B > C). Groups in D and X are never exported.
